{"id":"word:hebrew:H4397","type":"word","title":"מַלְאָךְ","subtitle":"H4397 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a messenger ; specifically, of God, i.e. an angel (also a prophet, priest or teacher)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מַלְאָךְ (H4397) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 213 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מַלְאָךְ (malʼâk) means a messenger ; specifically, of God, i.e. an angel (also a prophet, priest or teacher) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 14 1."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מַלְאָךְ","transliteration":"malʼâk","pronunciation":"mal-awk'","strong":"H4397","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4397","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["מַלְאַ֣ךְ","מַלְאָכִ֔ים","מַלְאַ֥ךְ","הַ/מַּלְאָכִ֔ים","הַ/מַּלְאָ֖ךְ"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc",55],["HNcmpa",44],["HTd/Ncmsa",27],["HTd/Ncmpa",16],["HNcmsa",12],["HC/Ncmsc",11],["HNcmpc",10],["HNcmpc/Sp3ms",7],["HC/Ncmsa",5],["HR/Ncmsc",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"a messenger ; specifically, of God, i.e. an angel (also a prophet, priest or teacher)","usage":"ambassador, angel, king, messenger.","full":"H4397. malak מַלְאָךְ 214 noun masculine messenger ; — ׳מ Exod 23:20 48t.; construct מַלְאַךְ Gen 16:7 69t.; suffixes מַלְאָכִי Exod 23:23 3 t.; מַלְאָכוֺ Gen 24:7 , 40 ; plural מַלְאָכִים 32:4 63t. + מלאכים 2Sam 11:1 Kt ( Qr מלכים ); construct מַלְאֲכֵי Gen 28:12 11 t.; מַלְאָכֶיךָ Num 24:12 ; 2Kin 19:23 ; מַלְאָכֵכֵה Nahum 2:14 error for מַלְאָכֵכִי = מַלְאָכַיְכִי Ges § 91 , (2) Anm. 2 or &lt; for מַלְאָכֵךְ by dittograph from following הוֺי Kö ii. 1. 571 ). מַלְאָכָיו 2Chr 36:15 8 t.; — 1 messenger , a. one sent with a message Gen 32:4 8 t. J E; Deut 2:26 , (not in P); Judg 6:35 8 t.; 1Sam 6:21 51t. Samuel Kings, 1Chr 14:1 ; 19:2 , 16 ; 2Chr 18:12 ; 35:21 ; Neh 6:3 ; Job 1:14 ; Prov 13:17 ; 17:11 ; Isa 14:32 ; 18:2 ; 30:4 ; 37:9 , 14 ; Jer 27:3 ; Ezek 17:15 ; 23:16 , 40 ; 30:9 ; Nahum 2:14; שׁלום מלאכי , messengers of peace Isa 33:7 . b. a prophet Isa 42:19 ; 44:26 ; 2Chr 36:15-16 , Hag 1:13 ; the herald of the advent מלאכי Mal 3:1 . c. priest Mal 2:7 , probably Eccl 5:5 (RV angel ). d. || מֵלִיץ Job 33:23 , a messenger from God acting as an interpreter and declaring what is right ( angel of RV too specific). e. figurative ׳מ רָעִים messengers of evil Psa 78:49 ; ׳מ מות messenger of death Prov 16:14 ; || רוחות winds his messengers Psa 104:4 . 2 angel , as messenger of God, מלאכים with God in theophanies Gen 19:1 , 15 ; 28:12 ; 32:2 (JE), praising him; Psa 103:20 ; 148:2 ; in his sight not without error Job 4:18 charged with the care of the pious Psa 91:11 ; elsewhere singular sent to a prophet 1Kin 13:18 ; 19:5 , 7 ; 2Kin 1:3 , 15 ; Zech 1:9 18 t. in Zechariah 1-6; excellent, wise, powerful 1Sam 29:9 ; 2Sam 14:17 , 20 ; 19:28 ; Zech 12:8 ; encamping about the faithful Psa 34:8 ; chasing his enemies 35:5 ; 35:6 ; destroying by judgment of Yahweh 2Sam 24:16-17 , = 1Chr 21:12-30 ; 2Kin 19:35 = Isa 37:36 2Chr 32:21 . 3 the theophanic angel ׳מ ה֯א֠להים in the story of E: Gen 21:17 ; 31:11 ; Exod 14:19 , also in Judg 6:20 ; 13:6 , 9 ; ׳מ יהוה in the story of J: Gen 16:7 , 9 , 10 , 11 ; 22:11 , 15 ; Exod 3:2 ; Num 22:22-23 , 24 , 25 , 26 , 27 , 31 , 32 , 34 , 35 and in Judg 2:1 ; 2:4 ; 5:23 ; 6:11 ; 6:12 ; 6:21 (twice in verse); 6:22 (twice in verse); 13:3 , 13 , 15 , 16 (twice in verse); 13:17-18 , 20 (twice in verse); 13:21 ; הַמַּלְאָךְ Gen 48:16 (E); מַלְאָךְ Exod 23:20 (E), 33:2 ; Num 20:16 (JE), Hosea 12:5 ; מַלְאָכִי Exod 23:23 (E), 32:34 (J); מַלְאָכוֺ Gen 24:7 , 40 (J), ׳מ פניו Mal 3:1 (referring to the ancient מלאך ); ׳מ הכרית 3:1 (referring to the advent of ׳י for judgment, see Br MP 473 ). The theophanic angel is not mentioned in D and P. לאך (√ of following; Biblical Hebrew מַלְאָח לאך, ).","rootNote":"from an unused root meaning to despatch as a deputy;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]